{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2993","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2993","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2993\",\"parent_revision\":\"1f5228abc6cb572bdedd03f3270e36735db795dc6d09519cc35a7ee9a91280cb\",\"root_revision\":\"1f5228abc6cb572bdedd03f3270e36735db795dc6d09519cc35a7ee9a91280cb\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-19\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/SKILL.md` (the skill that teaches how to author new slash commands) presents the shell-injection-vulnerable `` !`command` `` pattern as canonical example, with free-text `$1` interpolated directly into the injected command line:\\n\\n```\\ngrep -n '!`.*\\\\$1' plugins/plugin-creator/skills/command-development/SKILL.md\\n204:Run tests: !`npm test $1`\\n220:1. Fetch PR: !`gh pr view $1`\\n```\\n\\nThis is the identical vulnerability class fixed twice this session (`work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` and `plugin-creator/lint/SKILL.md` in PR #2981; `.claude/commands/sessions.md` deleted in PR #2988). No automated check exists anywhere in the repo \u2014 no skilllint rule, no prek hook, no CI job \u2014 that would catch `$ARGUMENTS`/`$1`-`$9` being interpolated into an `` !`...` `` injection line. Every instance found so far was caught only by a manual, ad-hoc grep sweep during this session, and that sweep itself initially missed `.claude/commands/sessions.md` due to under-scoping (it searched only `SKILL.md` files, not `commands/*.md`).\\n\\nImpact: this doc actively teaches the vulnerable shape to whoever next scaffolds a new command by following it, and there is currently no mechanism \u2014 beyond another manual sweep \u2014 that would catch a new instance being introduced anywhere in the repo (skills, commands, or `.claude/commands/`).\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **command-development skill still teaches vulnerable $arguments-in-shell-injection pattern, and no automated check exists to catch a recurrence** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Workflow-quality review, 2026-08-18/19, re-verified live 2026-08-19\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-19\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"dd39a1c639f2f107da368ded81c7ed6da375c0123755b1a009cc1ac2e12c4355\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPgvqPQ\"}"}